FounderOS — Setup & Run
========================

Prerequisites: Node.js 20+, pnpm 10+ (npm install -g pnpm), PostgreSQL running

Quick start (auto):
  .\start.ps1

It will:
  1. Check prerequisites (Node, pnpm)
  2. Create .env from .env.example if missing (edit it first!)
  3. pnpm install
  4. Push DB schema
  5. Seed the database
  6. Start API server (port 5001) & frontend (port 5000)

Flags: .\start.ps1 -SkipInstall -SkipDbPush -SkipSeed

Step by step (manual):
  pnpm install
  Copy .env.example → .env, fill in DATABASE_URL + PUTER_AUTH_TOKEN
  pnpm --filter @workspace/db push
  pnpm --filter @workspace/scripts seed            (clean: departments + agents only)
  pnpm --filter @workspace/scripts seed -- --demo  (adds a demo sales pipeline to try the Sales agent)

No local Postgres? Run one in Docker (user/password/db must match DATABASE_URL):
  docker run -d --name founderos-db -e POSTGRES_USER=app247ho -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<pw> -e POSTGRES_DB=app247ho -p 5432:5432 postgres:16-alpine

Windows Git Bash note: set MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1 before BASE_PATH=/ or bash rewrites "/" to a Windows path.

Two terminals:
  Terminal 1: $env:PORT=5001; $env:DATABASE_URL="postgresql://..."; pnpm --filter @workspace/api-server dev
  Terminal 2: $env:PORT=5000; $env:BASE_PATH="/"; pnpm --filter @workspace/founder-os dev

Open http://localhost:5000

MVP scope (Sales-first):
  Live:        Command Center, EA Desk, Sales Desk (/sales), Departments, Leads, Projects, Tasks, Activity, Settings
  Coming soon: HQ, Reports, Automations, Revenue, Radar, Planner, Notes, Reminders, Meetings, Team
  Sales agent: scans the pipeline on boot + every 6h, drafts follow-ups for quiet deals, scores new leads,
               schedules a follow-up task when a proposal is sent. Ask the EA Desk "which deals are going quiet?"

Configure AI providers in Settings → AI Providers (or set keys in .env).
